        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $s$ km/h be the speed from Adelaide to Melbourne. The reverse-direction speed is $2s$ km/h. The full-route journey times are $\\frac{660}{s}$ h and $\\frac{660}{2s}$ h. Their difference is $3$ h.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{660}{s}-\\frac{660}{2s}&=3\\\\660-330&=3s\\\\330&=3s\\\\s&=110\\end{align*}$$\nThe train from Adelaide to Melbourne travels at $110$ km/h.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
